[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix. Read by cause, it held three problems. Engineering closed
#4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed and the `booking-v3` form is retired. The one-day moves
are not covered by either.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but one problem is still open: invites that land one day off (#3).
</Callout>

## The split

Counted the way the desk counts (`CauseTable`): each report under the cause it is filed by.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

The tickets:

- `parser`: [WraithNath/mega-what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/WraithNath/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1), fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`)
- `hint`: [WraithNath/mega-what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/WraithNath/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2), won't fix: `booking-v3` form retired
- `one-day`: [WraithNath/mega-what-it-shows#3](https://github.com/WraithNath/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3), open

## What each problem is

1. **`parser`**: the shared parser read dates month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes the
   day first, so 7 April came out as 4 July.
2. **`hint`**: `booking-v3` printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date. Day-first people typed the month
   first as told, and the form read it day first. Only form reports from `booking-v3` tenants.
3. **`one-day`**: the desk read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). Day and month are
   right, but the date is a day off, and in one report it differs between Lisbon and Toronto. A swap
   can't do that, so the parser fix doesn't touch it. Likely a time-zone or date-boundary bug.

Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, so it isn't used here. The tenant directory
decides.

## For the desk

- Before you merge a report into a big ticket, check it has the same cause, not the same subject.
- A one-day move isn't a swap. New ones go to #3, not to a parser ticket.

